{
  "_comment": [
    "The answer key. Every probe is put to the real agent as a natural-language",
    "question with the same fixed preamble; the arm decides only how the agent",
    "can reach the repository, never what it is asked.",
    "",
    "`must_contain` is a list of GROUPS. A group is satisfied when any one of",
    "its alternatives appears in the answer, because the agent writes prose and",
    "there is more than one correct way to say a thing. All groups must be",
    "satisfied for the probe to count as answered.",
    "",
    "`must_not_contain` names superseded or decoy values. At the agent level a",
    "mention is not a failure: a good answer often lists what it ruled out. It",
    "counts as contamination only when the stale value is asserted ahead of the",
    "correct one -- the stale string appears and the correct string either does",
    "not appear at all or appears later.",
    "",
    "`needs` names a capability the probe cannot be answered without. It is not",
    "used to excuse an arm any more: whether the agent finds another route is",
    "exactly what is being measured. It survives as a label so misses can be",
    "grouped by what they demanded.",
    "",
    "`search` is the pattern the prompt-free ladder issues. The agent never",
    "sees it."
  ],
